{
  "readme": [
    "The shared x-rules corpus (morph#176). ONE file, TWO readers:",
    "  tests/test_forms_rule_corpus.cpp          -- morph::forms::allRulesSatisfied",
    "  src/qt/forms/tests/tst_DynamicFormRuleCorpus.qml -- a real DynamicForm",
    "Neither owns the cases, so the two evaluators cannot be pinned to",
    "different case lists. See docs/spec/forms/forms.md, 'Two evaluators, one",
    "corpus'.",
    "",
    "'schemas' holds verbatim schemaJson<A>() output, as TEXT. Storing it as a",
    "JSON string (not an inline object) is deliberate: the renderer parses the",
    "text it is served, and parsing is what rounds an int64 literal past 2^53.",
    "An inline object would be re-serialised by the writer and the corpus could",
    "not express that case at all.",
    "",
    "REGENERATE: the C++ test asserts every 'schemas' entry equals the current",
    "schemaJson<A>() byte-for-byte and prints the expected text on mismatch.",
    "Fixtures live in tests/forms_rule_corpus.hpp.",
    "",
    "'state' maps a wire field name to the TEXT a user would have typed; an",
    "absent field is unengaged. 'ready' is the submit gate both evaluators must",
    "agree on. 'visible'/'readonly' are the presentation expectations for the",
    "two kinds that never gate; only the renderer can assert them."
  ],
